After installing Vivado and Veriletor

run the following command

\rm -rf obj_dir zap.vcd*; verilator --trace-fst --binary --timing --exe --build -Wno-CMPCONST -Wno-WIDTHEXPAND -j $(nproc) -f file_list --top-module zap_test
./obj_dir/Vzap_test //To run
vcd2fst zap.vcd zap.fst //To reduce vcd file size
gtkwave zap.fst/vcd

This will run uart test at 192 baud, 1 stop bit, no parity and no flow control.

DDR3
----
1. sys_clk_i 6ns clock and clk_ref_i is 5ns clock.

./xsim_run_ddr3.sh 
xsim -R zap_test
gtkwave zap.vcd &
mac_xilinx.gtkw

Misc
----
\rm -rf eth_tb_phy.log zap.vcd zap_test.wdb xsim.* xelab.*
